# Who gets asked to look at a change.
#
# Review is not required to merge — this project has one maintainer, and a rule that
# blocks every pull request on an approval nobody can give is a rule that gets switched
# off. What this file does is make the request automatic, so a change to the parts below
# cannot land without the maintainer having been shown it.
#
# The paths listed separately are the ones where a mistake is not recoverable by editing
# a file afterwards.

*                                   @thiagoluga

# The quarantine is the only place in this project that removes a user's files. Every
# defect here costs somebody a website, and two have been found already: a copy that was
# verified after the unlink rather than before, and a vault the restore could not read.
/internal/quarantine/               @thiagoluga

# The verdict engine decides what gets quarantined. It is deliberately ignorant of which
# engine produced a vote (Principle VI); a change that teaches it one is a change to the
# project's shape, not to a file.
/internal/verdict/                  @thiagoluga

# The release key travels in these, and the panel is an administrative surface on a
# public URL.
/internal/selfupdate/               @thiagoluga
/internal/web/                      @thiagoluga
/.github/workflows/release.yml      @thiagoluga
/tools/release-key/                 @thiagoluga
/tools/verify-release/              @thiagoluga

# The catalogue ships third-party rules that decide what gets quarantined on somebody
# else's account. CI checks the digest is real; it cannot read the rules.
/catalog/                           @thiagoluga

# The rules the project is held to.
/.specify/memory/constitution.md    @thiagoluga
/DECISIONS.md                       @thiagoluga
/SECURITY.md                        @thiagoluga
